window.QDATA_1 = [{"id":"nb1","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2026 1F Q4","q":"(a) Write in words the number 32060. (b) Write in figures the number two hundred and four thousand, five hundred and twelve. (c) Write 9547 correct to the nearest hundred. (d) State the value of the 8 in 1.487. (e) Write these numbers in order of size, smallest first: 3.6, 3.006, 3.61, 3.601, 3.06","answer":"(a) thirty-two thousand and sixty (b) 204512 (c) 9500 (d) 8 hundredths (e) 3.006, 3.06, 3.6, 3.601, 3.61","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb2","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2026 1F Q8","q":"(a) Write 75 as a fraction of 125, in simplest form. (b) Write 21/105 as a percentage. (c) Write 4% as a decimal.","answer":"(a) 3/5 (b) 20% (c) 0.04","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb3","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2026 1F Q18","q":"Show that 4 1/7 - 2 3/5 = 1 19/35","answer":"4 1/7 = 29/7 = 145/35, 2 3/5 = 13/5 = 91/35, so 145/35 - 91/35 = 54/35 = 1 19/35","level":"easy","steps":["4 1/7 = 29/7 and 2 3/5 = 13/5","Common denominator 35: 29/7 = 145/35, 13/5 = 91/35","145/35 - 91/35 = 54/35 = 1 19/35"],"qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb4","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2026 2F Q4","q":"(a) Write 9/10 as a decimal. (b) A shape is made of 24 squares (3 rows of 8). Shade 3/8 of the shape. (c) Which of 2/3, 5/9, 11/16, 9/17 gives a terminating decimal? (d) A number machine does ÷6 then +7. Work out the output when the input is 48.","answer":"(a) 0.9 (b) shade any 9 of the 24 squares (3/8 × 24 = 9) (c) 11/16 (= 0.6875, since 16 = 2^4) (d) 48 ÷ 6 = 8, 8 + 7 = 15","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb5","topic":"numbers","ref":"Nov 2025 1F Q1","q":"(a) Write in figures the number six thousand, seven hundred and five. (b) Write these numbers in order of size, smallest first: 567, 498, 512, 427, 531. (c) State the value of the 7 in 0.3785. (d) Write down the multiple of 6 that is between 19 and 29. (e) Write down a prime number that is between 30 and 40.","answer":"(a) 6705 (b) 427, 498, 512, 531, 567 (c) 7 thousandths (d) 24 (e) 31 (or 37)","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb6","topic":"numbers","ref":"Nov 2025 1F Q3","q":"A number line runs from 630 to 650 with small ticks every 2. An arrow points to a value just before 640. (a) Write down the number marked with the arrow. (b) On a number line from 5000 to 7000, mark where 6750 would go. (c) A line AB is drawn - measure its length in cm with a ruler. (d) Draw an angle of 68° at a point X.","answer":"(a) 638 (b) three-quarters of the way from 6000 to 7000 (c) measure directly against the printed line with a ruler (d) use a protractor to draw 68° accurately","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb7","topic":"numbers","ref":"Nov 2025 1F Q5","q":"(a) A shape is made of 18 squares (3 rows of 6). Shade 1/6 of this shape. (b) Write 45/75 as a fraction in its simplest form. (c) Write 2/5 as a decimal. (d) There are 80 children in a playground. 1/5 of the children are wearing white T-shirts. Calculate the number of these children who are not wearing white T-shirts.","answer":"(a) shade any 3 of the 18 squares (b) 3/5 (c) 0.4 (d) 1/5 × 80 = 16 wearing white, so 80 - 16 = 64 not wearing white","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb8","topic":"numbers","ref":"Nov 2025 2F Q1","q":"A table shows distances travelled by six birds: Northern wheatear 28349 km, Arctic tern 95786 km, Pectoral sandpiper 27948 km, Sooty shearwater 64321 km, Pied wheatear 17582 km, Bar-tailed godwit 13496 km. (a) Which bird travelled the greatest distance? (b) Write 64321 correct to the nearest thousand. (c) Work out the difference between the distance travelled by the Northern wheatear and the Pied wheatear.","answer":"(a) Arctic tern (95786 km) (b) 64000 (c) 28349 - 17582 = 10767 km","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb9","topic":"numbers","ref":"Nov 2025 2F Q5","q":"(a) Write these decimals in order of size, smallest first: 0.67, 0.078, 0.7, 0.76, 0.706. (b) Write 0.62 as a percentage. (c) Which of 1/3, 2/7, 4/9, 3/5 can be written as a terminating decimal?","answer":"(a) 0.078, 0.67, 0.7, 0.706, 0.76 (b) 62% (c) 3/5 (= 0.6)","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb10","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2025 1F Q1","q":"(a) 475 + ? = 1200 (b) 180 × ? = 5760 (c) Using the digits 7, 4, 8, 5 once each: (i) write the smallest possible number, (ii) write the largest possible even number.","answer":"(a) 725 (b) 32 (c)(i) 4578 (ii) 8754","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb11","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2025 1F Q5","q":"(a) Write 0.6 as a percentage. (b) Write 19/100 as a decimal. (c) A 4x5 grid of 20 squares has 19 shaded (1 unshaded square in the top-left). What fraction of the shape is shaded, in simplest form?","answer":"(a) 60% (b) 0.19 (c) 19/20","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb12","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2025 1F Q13","q":"Show that 3/7 + 1/4 = 19/28","answer":"3/7 = 12/28, 1/4 = 7/28, so 12/28 + 7/28 = 19/28","level":"easy","steps":["Common denominator 28: 3/7 = 12/28, 1/4 = 7/28","12/28 + 7/28 = 19/28"],"qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb13","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2025 2F Q1","q":"A table shows areas of South American countries: Paraguay 406752, Suriname 163800, Uruguay 173626, Venezuela 926690, Chile 756100 (km^2). (a) Which country has the largest area? (b) Write 163800 in words. (c) State the value of the 7 in 406752. (d) Write 173626 correct to the nearest thousand. (e) Work out the difference between the area of Chile and the area of Uruguay.","answer":"(a) Venezuela (926690) (b) one hundred and sixty-three thousand, eight hundred (c) 7 hundreds (700) (d) 174000 (e) 756100 - 173626 = 582474","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb14","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2025 2F Q4","q":"A number line runs from 74 to 76 with small ticks every 0.2. An arrow points just after 75. (a) Write down the number marked with the arrow. (b) On a number line from 260 to 300, mark where 265 would go.","answer":"(a) 75.2 (b) halfway between 260 and 270","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb15","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2025 2F Q6","q":"(a) Write 19/5 as a mixed number. (b) Circle the two fractions that are equivalent: 19/20, 4/5, 20/24, 28/35, 5/9. (c) Write 0.3 as a fraction.","answer":"(a) 3 4/5 (b) 4/5 and 28/35 (both equal 0.8) (c) 3/10","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb16","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2025 2F Q13","q":"Work out the value of (9.75 - 1.4^2) / (9.2 + sqrt(6.3)). Write down all the figures on your calculator display.","answer":"(9.75 - 1.96) / (9.2 + 2.509980...) = 7.79 / 11.709980... = 0.66525... ≈ 0.6653","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb17","topic":"numbers","ref":"Nov 2024 1F Q1","q":"A table shows the lengths of five road tunnels: Arlberg 13972, Hsuehshan 12940, Laerdal 24512, St Gotthard 16918, Jinpingshan 17540 (metres). (a) Which tunnel has the greatest length? (b) Write down the value of the 9 in 13972. (c) One tunnel, rounded to the nearest thousand, is 17000 m - which tunnel? (d) Write 12940 in words. (e) Work out the total length of the Arlberg and Jinpingshan tunnels.","answer":"(a) Laerdal (24512 m) (b) 9 units (c) St Gotthard (16918 → 17000) (d) twelve thousand, nine hundred and forty (e) 13972 + 17540 = 31512 m","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb18","topic":"numbers","ref":"Nov 2024 2F Q1","q":"(a) Write 7823 correct to the nearest hundred. (b)(i) 0.4 × ? = 4000 (ii) 3600 ÷ ? = 3.6 (c) Write down four factors of 18. (d) Which one of 6, 12, 17, 22, 27 is a prime number?","answer":"(a) 7800 (b)(i) 10000 (ii) 1000 (c) e.g. 1, 2, 3, 6 (d) 17","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb19","topic":"numbers","ref":"Nov 2024 2F Q13","q":"(a) Use your calculator to work out (7.93 - 2.34^2)/0.14. Give your answer as a decimal, writing down all the figures on your calculator display. (b) Write your answer to part (a) correct to one decimal place.","answer":"(a) (7.93 - 5.4756)/0.14 = 2.4544/0.14 = 17.531428571... (b) 17.5","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb20","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2024 1F Q1","q":"A table shows shoreline lengths of seven lakes: Nasser 8947, Kentucky 3808, Saimaa 13600, Volta 4763, Huron 6124, Inari 2758, Superior 4361 (km). (a) Which lake has the longest shoreline? (b) Write 6124 in words. (c) The shoreline of Lake Nasser is longer than Lake Inari's - how much longer? (d) State the value of the 6 in 4763. (e) Two numbers round to 4000 to the nearest thousand - which two?","answer":"(a) Saimaa (13600) (b) six thousand, one hundred and twenty-four (c) 8947 - 2758 = 6189 km (d) 60 (6 tens) (e) Kentucky (3808) and Superior (4361)","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb21","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2024 2F Q3","q":"(a) Write in order of size, smallest first: -77, 39, -89, 43, -6. (b) Write these decimals in order of size, smallest first: 0.134, 0.12, 0.145, 0.017, 0.3. (c) Write 0.7 as a percentage. (d) Write 27/100 as a decimal. (e) There are 60 plants on a stall; 7/10 are vegetable plants. Work out how many are not vegetable plants.","answer":"(a) -89, -77, -6, 39, 43 (b) 0.017, 0.12, 0.134, 0.145, 0.3 (c) 70% (d) 0.27 (e) 7/10 × 60 = 42 vegetable, so 60 - 42 = 18 are not","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb22","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2024 2F Q6","q":"There are 150 animals on a farm: 19 sheep, 32 goats, 3 dogs, and the rest chickens. Write the number of chickens as a fraction of the total number of animals, in simplest form.","answer":"Chickens = 150 - 19 - 32 - 3 = 96, so fraction = 96/150 = 16/25","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb23","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2024 2F Q16","q":"Use your calculator to work out the value of 17.9/(8.61 + 2.36) - 1.2^2. Give your answer as a decimal, writing down all the figures on your calculator display.","answer":"17.9/10.97 - 1.44 = 1.631722... - 1.44 = 0.191722...","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb24","topic":"numbers","ref":"Nov 2023 1F Q5","q":"A shape is made of 12 squares (2 rows of 6). (a) Shade 2/3 of the shape. (b) Write 3/10 as a percentage. (c) Write 48/150 as a fraction in its simplest form. (d) Write 46/7 as a mixed number.","answer":"(a) shade any 8 of the 12 squares (2/3 × 12 = 8) (b) 30% (c) 8/25 (d) 6 4/7","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb25","topic":"numbers","ref":"Nov 2023 2F Q1","q":"A table shows weight of sugar produced by five countries: Japan 72900, Barbados 15745, Kenya 592668, Gabon 23787, Malaysia 28149 (tonnes). (a) Write 28149 in words. (b) Which country produced the greatest weight of sugar? (c) State the value of the 8 in 23787. (d) Write 15745 correct to the nearest thousand.","answer":"(a) twenty-eight thousand, one hundred and forty-nine (b) Kenya (592668) (c) 8 tens (80) (d) 16000","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb26","topic":"numbers","ref":"Nov 2023 2F Q3","q":"(a) Write 0.03 as a fraction. (b) Write 0.9 as a percentage. (c) Write these decimals in order of size, smallest first: 0.4, 0.48, 0.204, 0.24, 0.408. (d) Work out 0.93 + 7/10, giving your answer as a decimal.","answer":"(a) 3/100 (b) 90% (c) 0.204, 0.24, 0.4, 0.408, 0.48 (d) 0.93 + 0.7 = 1.63","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb27","topic":"numbers","ref":"Nov 2023 2F Q14","q":"Work out the value of (5.2^2 + 8.7) / sqrt(14.5). Write down all the figures on your calculator display.","answer":"(27.04 + 8.7)/3.807886... = 35.74/3.807886... = 9.38603...","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb28","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2023 1F Q1","q":"A shape is made of 15 squares (3 rows of 5). (a) Shade 4/5 of this shape. (b) Write 27/36 as a fraction in its simplest form. (c) Write 3/100 as a decimal. (d) Write 7/50 as a percentage.","answer":"(a) shade any 12 of the 15 squares (4/5 × 15 = 12) (b) 3/4 (c) 0.03 (d) 14%","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb29","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2023 2F Q1","q":"(a) Write in figures the number seven thousand and fifty-four. (b) Write 78263 correct to the nearest 100. (c) State the value of the 7 in 673000. (d) 9 × ? = 18000 (e) 53.7 ÷ ? = 0.00537","answer":"(a) 7054 (b) 78300 (c) 7 ten-thousands (70000) (d) 2000 (e) 10000","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb30","topic":"numbers","ref":"Jan 2023 1F Q1","q":"A table shows word counts and years for six Shakespeare plays. (a) Which play has the greatest number of words (Hamlet 30557)? (b) Two plays were written in the same year (1599) - name them. (c) Othello has 9329 more words than Macbeth (17121) - work out the number of words in Othello. (d) Write 21055 in words.","answer":"(a) Hamlet (b) Henry V and Julius Caesar (both 1599) (c) 17121 + 9329 = 26450 (d) twenty-one thousand and fifty-five","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb31","topic":"numbers","ref":"Jan 2023 1F Q4","q":"(a) Write 0.8 as a percentage. (b) State the value of the 3 in 4.7634. (c) Write these decimals in order of size, smallest first: 0.204, 0.24, 0.04, 0.2, 0.042. (d) Write 25.78621 correct to 2 decimal places. (e) Find the square root of 1296.","answer":"(a) 80% (b) 3 hundredths (c) 0.04, 0.042, 0.2, 0.204, 0.24 (d) 25.79 (e) 36","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb32","topic":"numbers","ref":"Jan 2023 2F Q1","q":"Four cards show 5, 7, 6, 3, arranged to make 5763. Using each card once: (a) make the smallest possible number. (b) make the largest possible even number. (c) arrange two cards to make a prime number. (d) arrange two cards to make a multiple of 8.","answer":"(a) 3567 (b) 7536 (c) e.g. 37 (d) 56 (= 8 × 7)","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb33","topic":"numbers","ref":"Jan 2023 2F Q3","q":"A number scale runs from 540 to 560 with small ticks every 2. (a) Mark with an arrow the number 554. A second scale runs from 2000 to 4000 with ticks every 250, with an arrow pointing just before 3000. (b) Write down the number shown marked by the arrow.","answer":"(a) 554 is 2 small ticks right of 550 (b) 2750","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb34","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2022 1F Q1","q":"A table shows the age of seven cities: Cadiz 3124, Suzhou 2534, Jenin 4469, Istanbul 2704, Nanjing 2516, Gaziantep 5669, Alexandria 2351 (years). (a) Which city has the greatest age? (b) Write 2534 in words. (c) Write 2351 correct to the nearest ten. (d) Work out the difference between the age of Cadiz and Nanjing. (e) A millennium is 1000 years - what is the age of Jenin in whole millenniums?","answer":"(a) Gaziantep (5669) (b) two thousand, five hundred and thirty-four (c) 2350 (d) 3124 - 2516 = 608 (e) 4 whole millenniums (4469 ÷ 1000 = 4.469)","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb35","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2022 2FR Q1","q":"(a) Write these numbers in order of size, smallest first: 202, 58, 123, 7, 180. (b) Write these numbers in order of size, smallest first: 0.155, 1.5, 0.15, 0.015, 1.15. (c) Write in figures the number five thousand two hundred and three. (d) State the value of the 6 in 2468.","answer":"(a) 7, 58, 123, 180, 202 (b) 0.015, 0.15, 0.155, 1.15, 1.5 (c) 5203 (d) 6 tens (60)","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb36","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2022 2FR Q3","q":"A protractor-style scale runs from 3.7 to 3.8 with 10 small divisions, with an arrow near the top pointing to the 6th division. (a) Write down the number marked with the arrow. (b) On a scale from 0 to 0.1 (ticks every 0.01), mark with an arrow the number 0.04.","answer":"(a) 3.76 (b) the 4th tick from 0","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb37","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2022 2FR Q1 (b)","q":"(a) Write 0.3 as a percentage. (b) Write 29/100 as a decimal. (c) Write 17/20 as a decimal. (d) Order smallest first: -7, 8, -9, 16, -3. (e) Order smallest first: 0.044, 0.104, 0.04, 0.009, 0.2. (f) There are 400 cars in a car park; 3/10 are grey. Work out how many are not grey.","answer":"(a) 30% (b) 0.29 (c) 0.85 (d) -9, -7, -3, 8, 16 (e) 0.009, 0.04, 0.044, 0.104, 0.2 (f) 3/10 × 400 = 120 grey, so 400 - 120 = 280 not grey","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb38","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2022 2FR Q8","q":"Mairi has 200 flowers: 37 white, 25 yellow, 42 pink, and the rest red. Express the number of red flowers as a fraction of the total, in simplest form.","answer":"Red = 200 - 37 - 25 - 42 = 96, fraction = 96/200 = 12/25","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb39","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2022 2FR Q15","q":"Use your calculator to work out (5.21 + 6.37)/9.8 + 8.3^2. Write down all the figures on your calculator display.","answer":"11.58/9.8 + 68.89 = 1.181632... + 68.89 = 70.071632...","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb40","topic":"numbers","ref":"Jan 2022 1F Q1","q":"A table shows average annual rainfall for five countries: Colombia 3240, Jamaica 2051, Brazil 1761, Japan 1668, France 867 (mm). (a) Write 2051 in words. (b) Write 1668 correct to the nearest hundred. (c) Colombia's rainfall is more than Brazil's - by how much? (d) Nigeria's rainfall was 283 mm more than France's - work out Nigeria's average rainfall.","answer":"(a) two thousand and fifty-one (b) 1700 (c) 3240 - 1761 = 1479 mm (d) 867 + 283 = 1150 mm","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb41","topic":"numbers","ref":"Jan 2022 1F Q3","q":"A rectangle is made of 20 squares (2 rows of 10). (a) Shade 0.7 of the rectangle. (b) State the value of the 2 in 3.289. (c) Write 5/8 as a decimal. (d) Order smallest first: 2.803, 2.008, 2.081, 2.83, 2.8.","answer":"(a) shade any 14 of the 20 squares (0.7 × 20 = 14) (b) 2 hundredths (c) 0.625 (d) 2.008, 2.081, 2.8, 2.803, 2.83","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb42","topic":"numbers","ref":"Jan 2022 1F Q9","q":"(a) Write 39/150 as a percentage. (b) There are 30 dogs in boarding kennels; 12 are brown. What fraction are not brown, in simplest form? (c) Show that 4/9 + 1/6 = 11/18","answer":"(a) 26% (b) (30-12)/30 = 18/30 = 3/5 (c) 8/18 + 3/18 = 11/18","level":"easy","steps":["4/9 = 8/18 and 1/6 = 3/18","8/18 + 3/18 = 11/18"],"qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb43","topic":"numbers","ref":"Jan 2022 2FR Q1","q":"A table shows forest area for six countries: South Africa 92410, Denmark 5871, El Salvador 2870, Bahamas 5150, Jamaica 3371, Syria 4910 (km^2). (a) Which country has the least forest area? (b) State the value of the 4 in 92410. (c) Two countries round to 5000 (nearest thousand) - name them. (d) Write 3371 in words.","answer":"(a) El Salvador (2870) (b) 4 hundreds (400) (c) Bahamas (5150) and Syria (4910) (d) three thousand, three hundred and seventy-one","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb44","topic":"numbers","ref":"Jan 2022 2FR Q5","q":"(a) Work out 4/5 of 80. (b) Write 9/20 as a decimal. (c) Which of 1/3, 2/9, 3/8, 4/11 gives a terminating decimal? (d) Write 11/4 as a mixed number in its simplest form. (e) Use cube/square/prime/negative to describe: a number that is both a factor pair type and only divisible by 1 and itself.","answer":"(a) 64 (b) 0.45 (c) 3/8 (= 0.375, since 8 = 2^3) (d) 2 3/4 (e) prime","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb45","topic":"numbers","ref":"Jan 2022 2FR Q1 (b)","q":"A square is split into 4 triangles by its diagonals. (a) Shade 1/4 of the square. A rhombus split into 4 triangles has 2 opposite triangles shaded. (b) What fraction of the rhombus is shaded? (c) Write 0.9 as a fraction.","answer":"(a) shade any 1 of the 4 triangles (b) 1/2 (c) 9/10","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb46","topic":"numbers","ref":"Jan 2022 2FR Q7","q":"3/8 of the members of a squash club are children. 5/6 of these children are right-handed. What fraction of the members of the squash club are right-handed children, in simplest form?","answer":"3/8 × 5/6 = 15/48 = 5/16","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb47","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2026 2F Q15","q":"Show that 4/5 × 1/8 = 1/10","answer":"4/5 × 1/8 = 4/40 = 1/10","level":"medium","steps":["4/5 × 1/8 = 4/40","4/40 = 1/10"],"qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb48","topic":"numbers","ref":"Nov 2025 1F Q22","q":"Show that 3 5/7 + 1 2/3 = 5 8/21","answer":"5/7 + 2/3 = 15/21 + 14/21 = 29/21 = 1 8/21, so 3 + 1 + 1 8/21 = 5 8/21","level":"medium","steps":["5/7 = 15/21 and 2/3 = 14/21","15/21 + 14/21 = 29/21 = 1 8/21","3 + 1 8/21 + 1 = 5 8/21"],"qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb49","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2025 2F Q14","q":"A company makes 125 cars each hour for 9 hours a day, for 5 days each week. 24% of the cars the company makes are red. Work out the number of red cars made each week.","answer":"125 × 9 × 5 = 5625 cars per week; 24% of 5625 = 1350 red cars","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb50","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2025 2F Q20","q":"Show that 7 1/3 - 3 4/7 = 3 16/21","answer":"7 1/3 = 22/3 = 154/21, 3 4/7 = 25/7 = 75/21, so 154/21 - 75/21 = 79/21 = 3 16/21","level":"medium","steps":["7 1/3 = 22/3 = 154/21 and 3 4/7 = 25/7 = 75/21","154/21 - 75/21 = 79/21 = 3 16/21"],"qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb51","topic":"numbers","ref":"Nov 2024 1F Q15","q":"Rema buys 140 plants. 35% cost $6 each, 1/4 cost $8 each, and the rest cost $10 each. Work out the total cost of the 140 plants.","answer":"35% of 140 = 49 plants × $6 = $294; 1/4 of 140 = 35 plants × $8 = $280; rest = 140-49-35=56 plants × $10 = $560; total = $294+$280+$560 = $1134","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb52","topic":"numbers","ref":"Nov 2024 2F Q4","q":"A rectangle is made of 21 squares (3 rows of 7). (a) Shade 3/7 of the rectangle. Here are five fractions: 33/43, 18/24, 16/20, 21/27, 12/16. (b) Write down the two fractions that are equivalent to 3/4. (c) Write 24/7 as a mixed number. (d) Write 9/10 as a percentage. There are 80 crayons in a box; 2/5 are red. (e) Work out the number of crayons that are not red.","answer":"(a) shade any 9 of the 21 squares (3/7 × 21 = 9) (b) 18/24 and 12/16 (c) 3 3/7 (d) 90% (e) 2/5 × 80 = 32 red, so 80 - 32 = 48 not red","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb53","topic":"numbers","ref":"Nov 2024 2F Q17","q":"Show that 1 5/7 × 2 3/16 = 3 3/4","answer":"12/7 × 35/16 = 420/112 = 15/4 = 3 3/4","level":"medium","steps":["1 5/7 = 12/7 and 2 3/16 = 35/16","12/7 × 35/16 = 420/112 = 15/4 = 3 3/4"],"qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb54","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2024 2F Q20","q":"Show that 2 4/7 × 3 1/9 = 8","answer":"18/7 × 28/9 = 504/63 = 8","level":"medium","steps":["2 4/7 = 18/7 and 3 1/9 = 28/9","18/7 × 28/9 = 504/63 = 8"],"qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb55","topic":"numbers","ref":"Nov 2023 2F Q22","q":"Show that 3 3/7 ÷ 2 2/3 = 1 2/7","answer":"24/7 ÷ 8/3 = 24/7 × 3/8 = 72/56 = 9/7 = 1 2/7","level":"medium","steps":["3 3/7 = 24/7 and 2 2/3 = 8/3","24/7 × 3/8 = 72/56 = 9/7 = 1 2/7"],"qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb56","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2023 2F Q8","q":"A hall has 26 rows of seats with 14 seats in each row. Annie sells tickets for 3/4 of the seats for a concert, at 15 euros each. Work out the total amount Annie gets from selling tickets.","answer":"26 × 14 = 364 seats; 3/4 × 364 = 273 tickets; 273 × 15 = 4095 euros","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb57","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2023 2F Q17","q":"Show that 4 2/3 ÷ 1 1/5 = 3 8/9","answer":"14/3 ÷ 6/5 = 14/3 × 5/6 = 70/18 = 35/9 = 3 8/9","level":"medium","steps":["4 2/3 = 14/3 and 1 1/5 = 6/5","14/3 × 5/6 = 70/18 = 35/9 = 3 8/9"],"qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb58","topic":"numbers","ref":"Jan 2023 1F Q12","q":"(a) Show that 7/8 - 5/12 = 11/24. (b) Find the highest common factor (HCF) of 130 and 208.","answer":"(a) 21/24 - 10/24 = 11/24 (b) 130 = 2×5×13, 208 = 2^4×13, so HCF = 2×13 = 26","level":"medium","steps":["7/8 = 21/24 and 5/12 = 10/24","21/24 - 10/24 = 11/24"],"qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb59","topic":"numbers","ref":"Jan 2023 2F Q16","q":"Show that 3 5/7 ÷ 1 5/8 = 2 2/7","answer":"26/7 ÷ 13/8 = 26/7 × 8/13 = 208/91 = 16/7 = 2 2/7","level":"medium","steps":["3 5/7 = 26/7 and 1 5/8 = 13/8","26/7 × 8/13 = 208/91 = 16/7 = 2 2/7"],"qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb60","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2022 2F Q20","q":"Show that 5 1/3 - 2 6/7 = 2 10/21","answer":"16/3 - 20/7 = 112/21 - 60/21 = 52/21 = 2 10/21","level":"medium","steps":["5 1/3 = 16/3 = 112/21 and 2 6/7 = 20/7 = 60/21","112/21 - 60/21 = 52/21 = 2 10/21"],"qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb61","topic":"numbers","ref":"Jan 2022 2FR Q16","q":"(a) Show that 3/8 ÷ 27/32 = 4/9. (b) Show that 5/6 - 3/8 = 11/24","answer":"(a) 3/8 × 32/27 = 96/216 = 4/9 (b) 20/24 - 9/24 = 11/24","level":"medium","steps":["(a) 3/8 ÷ 27/32 = 3/8 × 32/27 = 96/216 = 4/9","(b) 5/6 = 20/24 and 3/8 = 9/24, so 20/24 - 9/24 = 11/24"],"qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb62","topic":"numbers","ref":"Jan 2022 2F Q17","q":"Show that 6 3/4 ÷ 2 4/7 = 2 5/8","answer":"27/4 ÷ 18/7 = 27/4 × 7/18 = 189/72 = 21/8 = 2 5/8","level":"medium","steps":["6 3/4 = 27/4 and 2 4/7 = 18/7","27/4 × 7/18 = 189/72 = 21/8 = 2 5/8"],"qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb63","topic":"numbers","ref":"Nov 2025 2F Q20","q":"A box contains only 9 red bricks, 43 blue bricks, and some yellow bricks. 7/20 of the bricks are yellow. Each brick weighs 35 grams. Work out the total weight of the yellow bricks.","answer":"Non-yellow = 9+43 = 52 = 13/20 of total, so total = 52 × 20/13 = 80 bricks; yellow = 80-52 = 28 bricks; weight = 28 × 35 = 980 g","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb64","topic":"numbers","ref":"Jan 2023 2F Q13","q":"There are 380 students in a Sixth Form, split into Upper Sixth and Lower Sixth. The number in Upper Sixth is 20 fewer than in Lower Sixth. 2/5 of Upper Sixth study mathematics, and 32% of Lower Sixth study mathematics. Work out the total number of students who study mathematics.","answer":"Lower + Upper = 380, Upper = Lower - 20, so 2(Lower) - 20 = 380, Lower = 200, Upper = 180. Upper maths = 2/5×180=72. Lower maths = 32%×200=64. Total = 72+64 = 136","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb65","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2022 2FR Q15","q":"Kim spends $N. Of this she spends 40% on food, 1/4 on clothes, and the rest ($P) on petrol. Work out the ratio P:N in the form a:b where a and b are integers, in simplest form.","answer":"Petrol = 100% - 40% - 25% = 35%, so P:N = 35:100 = 7:20","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb66","topic":"numbers","ref":"Jan 2022 1F Q19","q":"Sarah makes and sells mugs. One day she makes 150 mugs at a total cost of £1140. Of these, 2/5 are small, 32% are medium, and the rest are large. She sells small mugs at £8.50, medium at £11.20, and large at £14.20, selling all 150 mugs. Work out her percentage profit, correct to the nearest whole number.","answer":"Small = 2/5×150=60, medium = 32%×150=48, large = 150-60-48=42. Revenue = 60×8.50+48×11.20+42×14.20 = 510+537.6+596.4 = £1644. Profit = 1644-1140=£504. % profit = 504/1140×100 ≈ 44%","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb67","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2026 2H Q17","q":"Use algebra to show that 0.5(39 recurring) = 89/165","answer":"Let x = 0.539393939... Then 1000x - 10x = 990x = 534, so x = 534/990 = 89/165","level":"medium","steps":["Let x = 0.5393939... (39 recurring)","10x = 5.393939..., 1000x = 539.393939...","1000x - 10x = 990x = 534, so x = 534/990 = 89/165"],"qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb68","topic":"numbers","ref":"Nov 2025 2H Q16","q":"Use algebra to show that 0.3(78 recurring) = 25/66","answer":"Let x = 0.378787878... Then 1000x - 10x = 990x = 375, so x = 375/990 = 25/66","level":"medium","steps":["Let x = 0.3787878... (78 recurring)","10x = 3.787878..., 1000x = 378.787878...","1000x - 10x = 990x = 375, so x = 375/990 = 25/66"],"qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb69","topic":"numbers","ref":"June 2025 2H Q18","q":"Use algebra to show that 0.(702 recurring) = 26/37","answer":"Let x = 0.702702702... Then 1000x - x = 999x = 702, so x = 702/999 = 26/37","level":"medium","steps":["Let x = 0.702702702... (702 recurring)","1000x = 702.702702...","1000x - x = 999x = 702, so x = 702/999 = 26/37"],"qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb70","topic":"numbers","ref":"Nov 2024 2H Q15","q":"Use algebra to show that 0.7(63 recurring) = 42/55","answer":"Let x = 0.763636363... Then 1000x - 10x = 990x = 756, so x = 756/990 = 42/55","level":"medium","steps":["Let x = 0.7636363... (63 recurring)","10x = 7.636363..., 1000x = 763.636363...","1000x - 10x = 990x = 756, so x = 756/990 = 42/55"],"qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb71","topic":"numbers","ref":"Jan 2023 2H Q16","q":"Use algebra to show that 0.4(38 recurring) = 217/495","answer":"Let x = 0.438383838... Then 1000x - 10x = 990x = 434, so x = 434/990 = 217/495","level":"hard","steps":["Let x = 0.4383838... (38 recurring)","10x = 4.383838..., 1000x = 438.383838...","1000x - 10x = 990x = 434, so x = 434/990 = 217/495"],"qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"nb72","topic":"numbers","ref":"Nov 2023 2H Q15","q":"(a) Use algebra to show that 0.3(72 recurring) = 41/110. (b) Express (√125 + √80)/√3 in the form √n where n is an integer.","answer":"(a) Let x = 0.372727272..., 1000x - 10x = 990x = 369, so x = 369/990 = 41/110 (b) √125=5√5, √80=4√5, sum=9√5; 9√5/√3 = 9√(5/3) = 9√15/3 = 3√15 = √135, so n = 135","level":"challenge","steps":["(a) x = 0.3727272...; 1000x=372.7272..., 10x=3.7272...; 990x=369; x=369/990=41/110","(b) √125 = 5√5, √80 = 4√5, so numerator = 9√5","9√5/√3 = 3√15 = √135, so n = 135"],"qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"ac1","topic":"accuracy","ref":"June 2026 1F Q11","q":"(a) Work out 12.5/1.4 - sqrt(10), writing down all figures on your calculator display. (b) Write your answer to part (a) correct to 2 significant figures.","answer":"(a) 8.928571... - 3.162278... = 5.766294... (b) 5.8","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"ac2","topic":"accuracy","ref":"Nov 2025 1F Q24","q":"The weight of a bag of apples is 475g correct to the nearest g. (a) Write down the lower bound of the weight. The height of a box is 120cm correct to the nearest 10cm. (b) Write down the upper bound for the height.","answer":"(a) 474.5 g (b) 125 cm","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"ac3","topic":"accuracy","ref":"Nov 2024 2F Q18","q":"The length of a table is measured as 1.4 metres correct to one decimal place. (a) Write down the upper bound of the length. (b) Write down the lower bound of the length.","answer":"(a) 1.45 m (b) 1.35 m","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"ac4","topic":"accuracy","ref":"June 2023 1F Q14","q":"(a) Work out the value of 9/12.4 + (5.3×2.8)/9.64. Give your answer as a decimal, writing down all figures on your calculator display. (b) Write your answer to part (a) correct to 3 significant figures.","answer":"(a) 0.725806... + 1.539419... = 2.265225... (b) 2.27","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"ac5","topic":"accuracy","ref":"Jan 2022 1F Q11","q":"(a) Use your calculator to work out 7.45/(4.3^2 - 2.9). Give your answer as a decimal, writing down all figures on your calculator display. (b) Write your answer to part (a) correct to 3 decimal places.","answer":"(a) 7.45/(18.49-2.9) = 7.45/15.59 = 0.477870... (b) 0.478","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"ac6","topic":"accuracy","ref":"Jan 2022 2F Q19","q":"Each side of a regular octagon has a length of 18mm, correct to the nearest 0.5mm. (a) Write down the lower bound of the length of each side. (b) Write down the upper bound of the length of each side.","answer":"(a) 17.75 mm (b) 18.25 mm","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"ac7","topic":"accuracy","ref":"Nov 2025 1F Q19","q":"By rounding each number to one significant figure, work out an estimate for the value of (2.11^2 × 58.9) / sqrt(8.859). Show your working clearly.","answer":"2.11²≈2²=4, 58.9≈60, √8.859≈√9=3, so estimate = 4×60/3 = 80","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Round: 2.11→2, 58.9→60, 8.859→9","Estimate = (2² × 60)/√9 = (4×60)/3 = 240/3 = 80"]},{"id":"ac8","topic":"accuracy","ref":"Nov 2024 1F Q16","q":"By rounding each number to one significant figure, work out an estimate for 31.4 × 48.7. Show your working clearly.","answer":"31.4≈30, 48.7≈50, so estimate = 30×50 = 1500","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Round: 31.4→30, 48.7→50","Estimate = 30 × 50 = 1500"]},{"id":"ac9","topic":"accuracy","ref":"Jan 2022 2F Q8","q":"By writing each value correct to one significant figure, work out an estimate for (8.23 × 181)/0.482. Show your working clearly.","answer":"8.23≈8, 181≈200, 0.482≈0.5, so estimate = (8×200)/0.5 = 1600/0.5 = 3200","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Round: 8.23→8, 181→200, 0.482→0.5","Estimate = (8×200)/0.5 = 1600/0.5 = 3200"]},{"id":"ac10","topic":"accuracy","ref":"Jan 2023 2F Q20","q":"The weight of a cake is 2.75 kg, correct to 2 decimal places. (a) Write down the lower bound of the weight. (b) Write down the upper bound of the weight. Penny worked out (81.3×59.2)/1.9^2 on her calculator and got 13332.29917, which is not sensible. (c) By rounding each number to one significant figure, work out a suitable estimate to show her answer is not sensible. Show your working clearly.","answer":"(a) 2.745 kg (b) 2.755 kg (c) 81.3≈80, 59.2≈60, 1.9²≈2²=4, estimate = (80×60)/4 = 1200, which is nowhere near 13332.3 — confirming her answer is wrong","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Round: 81.3→80, 59.2→60, 1.9→2","Estimate = (80×60)/2² = 4800/4 = 1200 — far from Penny's 13332.3, so her answer is not sensible"]},{"id":"ac11","topic":"accuracy","ref":"June 2024 2H Q19","q":"G = c/(2f - 3h), where c=8 correct to the nearest whole number, f=6.62 correct to 2 decimal places, h=1.2 correct to 1 decimal place. Work out the lower bound for the value of G, correct to 3 decimal places. Show your working clearly.","answer":"c_lower=7.5, f_upper=6.625, h_lower=1.15. Denominator max = 2(6.625)-3(1.15)=13.25-3.45=9.8. G_lower = 7.5/9.8 = 0.765 (3dp)","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Bounds: c∈[7.5,8.5], f∈[6.615,6.625], h∈[1.15,1.25]","To minimise G, use c lower and maximise denominator (f upper, h lower): 2(6.625)-3(1.15)=9.8","G_lower = 7.5/9.8 = 0.765 (3dp)"]},{"id":"ac12","topic":"accuracy","ref":"Nov 2023 2H Q17","q":"P = a(c+y), where a=8.3 correct to 2 significant figures, c=2 correct to 1 significant figure, y=15 correct to the nearest 5. Work out the upper bound for the value of P. Show your working clearly.","answer":"a_upper=8.35, c_upper=2.5, y_upper=17.5. P_upper = 8.35×(2.5+17.5) = 8.35×20 = 167","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Bounds: a∈[8.25,8.35], c∈[1.5,2.5], y∈[12.5,17.5]","P_upper = a_upper×(c_upper+y_upper) = 8.35×20 = 167"]},{"id":"ac13","topic":"accuracy","ref":"June 2022 2H Q18","q":"X = (2a-b)/f, where a=7.5 correct to 1 decimal place, b=3.42 correct to 2 decimal places, f=2 correct to the nearest whole number. Work out the upper bound of the value of X. Show your working clearly.","answer":"a_upper=7.55, b_lower=3.415, f_lower=1.5. Numerator max = 2(7.55)-3.415=11.685. X_upper = 11.685/1.5 = 7.79","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Bounds: a∈[7.45,7.55], b∈[3.415,3.425], f∈[1.5,2.5]","To maximise X: numerator upper (a upper, b lower) and denominator lower: 2(7.55)-3.415=11.685","X_upper = 11.685/1.5 = 7.79"]},{"id":"ac14","topic":"accuracy","ref":"Jan 2022 1H Q18","q":"A = w - x^2/y, where w=3.45 correct to 2 decimal places, x=1.9 correct to 1 decimal place, y=5 correct to the nearest whole number. Work out the lower bound of the value of A. Show your working clearly.","answer":"w_lower=3.445, x_upper=1.95, y_lower=4.5. x²/y max = 1.95²/4.5=3.8025/4.5=0.845. A_lower = 3.445-0.845 = 2.6","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Bounds: w∈[3.445,3.455], x∈[1.85,1.95], y∈[4.5,5.5]","To minimise A: w lower, and maximise x²/y (x upper, y lower): 1.95²/4.5=0.845","A_lower = 3.445 - 0.845 = 2.6"]},{"id":"ac15","topic":"accuracy","ref":"June 2026 1H Q20","q":"The final velocity, v m/s, of an object is given by v = 2(s/t) - u, where s=100 correct to the nearest integer, t=1.68 correct to 2 decimal places, u=0.5 correct to 1 decimal place. By considering bounds, work out the value of v to a suitable degree of accuracy. Show your working clearly.","answer":"v_lower = 2(99.5/1.685)-0.55 = 117.551..., v_upper = 2(100.5/1.675)-0.45 = 119.55. Both round to 120 (2 s.f.), so v = 120 m/s","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Bounds: s∈[99.5,100.5], t∈[1.675,1.685], u∈[0.45,0.55]","v_lower = 2(99.5/1.685)-0.55 ≈ 117.55","v_upper = 2(100.5/1.675)-0.45 = 119.55","Both bounds round to 120 (2 s.f.), so v = 120 m/s"]},{"id":"ac16","topic":"accuracy","ref":"Nov 2025 2H Q24","q":"D = n/(p-q), where n=10.3 correct to 1 decimal place, p=7.24 correct to 2 decimal places, q=4.39 correct to 2 decimal places. By considering bounds, work out the value of D to a suitable degree of accuracy. Show your working clearly.","answer":"D_lower = 10.25/(7.245-4.385) = 3.584, D_upper = 10.35/(7.235-4.395) = 3.644. Both round to 3.6 (2 s.f.), so D = 3.6","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Bounds: n∈[10.25,10.35], p∈[7.235,7.245], q∈[4.385,4.395]","D_lower = 10.25/(7.245-4.385) = 10.25/2.86 ≈ 3.584","D_upper = 10.35/(7.235-4.395) = 10.35/2.84 ≈ 3.644","Both round to 3.6 (2 s.f.), so D = 3.6"]},{"id":"ac17","topic":"accuracy","ref":"June 2025 2H Q22","q":"A square is cut from inside rectangle ABCD, shaded area X cm². AB=11.5cm correct to the nearest 0.5cm, BC=9.2cm correct to 2 significant figures, side of square=4.1cm correct to 2 significant figures. By considering bounds, work out the value of X to a suitable degree of accuracy. Show your working clearly.","answer":"X_lower = 11.25×9.15-4.15² = 85.72, X_upper = 11.75×9.25-4.05² = 92.29. Both round to 90 (1 s.f.), so X = 90 cm²","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Bounds: AB∈[11.25,11.75], BC∈[9.15,9.25], side∈[4.05,4.15]","X_lower = AB_lower×BC_lower - side_upper² = 11.25×9.15-4.15² ≈ 85.72","X_upper = AB_upper×BC_upper - side_lower² = 11.75×9.25-4.05² ≈ 92.29","Both round to 90 (1 s.f.), so X = 90 cm²"]},{"id":"ac18","topic":"accuracy","ref":"Nov 2024 1H Q21","q":"T = (x^2+y^2)/w, where x=28.4 correct to 1 decimal place, y=17 correct to 2 significant figures, w=90 correct to the nearest 5. Calculate the upper bound for the value of T, correct to 3 significant figures. Show your working clearly.","answer":"x_upper=28.45, y_upper=17.5, w_lower=87.5. Numerator=28.45²+17.5²=1115.65. T_upper=1115.65/87.5=12.75... ≈ 12.8","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Bounds: x∈[28.35,28.45], y∈[16.5,17.5], w∈[87.5,92.5]","T_upper = (x_upper²+y_upper²)/w_lower = (28.45²+17.5²)/87.5 = 1115.65/87.5 ≈ 12.75","T_upper ≈ 12.8 (3 s.f.)"]},{"id":"ac19","topic":"accuracy","ref":"June 2023 2H Q25","q":"A solid sphere has radius 2.8cm correct to 1 decimal place and mass Mπ grams where M=260 correct to 2 significant figures. Work out the upper bound for the density of the sphere, in g/cm³ correct to 2 decimal places. Show your working clearly.","answer":"Density = Mπ/((4/3)πr³) = 3M/(4r³). Upper bound: M_upper=265, r_lower=2.75. Density = 3(265)/(4×2.75³) = 795/83.1875 = 9.56 g/cm³","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Density = mass/volume = Mπ/((4/3)πr³) = 3M/(4r³) — the π cancels","Bounds: M∈[255,265], r∈[2.75,2.85]","To maximise density: M upper, r lower: 3(265)/(4×2.75³) = 795/83.1875 ≈ 9.56 g/cm³"]},{"id":"ac20","topic":"accuracy","ref":"Jan 2023 1H Q19","q":"The acceleration, a, of an object is given by a = (v-u)/t, where v=45.23 correct to 2 decimal places, u=5.12 correct to 2 decimal places, t=8.5 correct to 2 significant figures. By considering bounds, work out the value of a to a suitable degree of accuracy, giving a reason for your answer.","answer":"a_lower = (45.225-5.125)/8.55 = 4.690, a_upper = (45.235-5.115)/8.45 = 4.747. Both round to 4.7 (2 s.f.), so a = 4.7 — because both the lower and upper bound round to the same value at that accuracy","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Bounds: v∈[45.225,45.235], u∈[5.115,5.125], t∈[8.45,8.55]","a_lower = (45.225-5.125)/8.55 ≈ 4.690","a_upper = (45.235-5.115)/8.45 ≈ 4.747","Both round to 4.7 (2 s.f.), so a = 4.7 to that accuracy"]},{"id":"fa1","topic":"factorising","ref":"June 2024 2F Q27","q":"(i) Factorise x^2 + 9x - 22. (ii) Hence, solve x^2 + 9x - 22 = 0","answer":"(i) (x+11)(x-2) (ii) x = -11 or x = 2","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"fa2","topic":"factorising","ref":"Jan 2023 2F Q7","q":"(a) Simplify c×c×c×c×c. (b) Solve 5+x=12. (c) Solve y/6=3. (d) Expand 5(2+3h). (e) Factorise g^2+7g","answer":"(a) c^5 (b) x=7 (c) y=18 (d) 10+15h (e) g(g+7)","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"fa3","topic":"factorising","ref":"June 2022 2FR Q9","q":"(a) Simplify a×a×a×a×a. (b) Simplify 8b×3c. (c) Expand 3(x+4). Q=5v^2-w. (d) Work out the value of Q when v=1/2 and w=1/4","answer":"(a) a^5 (b) 24bc (c) 3x+12 (d) Q=5(1/2)²-1/4=5/4-1/4=1","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"fa4","topic":"factorising","ref":"June 2022 2F Q27","q":"(i) Factorise x^2 + 5x - 24. (ii) Hence, solve x^2 + 5x - 24 = 0","answer":"(i) (x+8)(x-3) (ii) x = -8 or x = 3","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"fa5","topic":"factorising","ref":"June 2026 1F Q22","q":"(a) Expand 4e(2e-3). (b) Expand and simplify (f+3)(f-6). (c) Make x the subject of t=ax-2n. (d) On the number line, represent the inequality -1<y≤3","answer":"(a) 8e²-12e (b) f²-3f-18 (c) x=(t+2n)/a (d) open circle at -1, closed (filled) circle at 3, line shaded between them","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"fa6","topic":"factorising","ref":"Nov 2025 2F Q24","q":"(i) Factorise x^2 + 2x - 48. (ii) Hence, solve x^2 + 2x - 48 = 0","answer":"(i) (x+8)(x-6) (ii) x = -8 or x = 6","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"fa7","topic":"factorising","ref":"Nov 2024 1F Q25","q":"(a)(i) Factorise x^2+5x-24. (ii) Hence, solve x^2+5x-24=0. (b) Solve the inequality 3y+5>7y-10. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"(a)(i) (x+8)(x-3) (ii) x=-8 or x=3 (b) 3y+5>7y-10 → 15>4y → y<15/4 (3.75)","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(b) 3y+5 > 7y-10","5+10 > 7y-3y","15 > 4y, so y < 15/4"]},{"id":"fa8","topic":"factorising","ref":"June 2024 2F Q11","q":"(a) Simplify e×e×e×e×e. (b) Simplify m+m+m. (c) Simplify 3g^2+7g^2-4g^2. (d) Expand a(a+8). (e) Factorise 15x+20. Sophia sells d packs (3 cars each) and h boxes (5 cars each) of toy cars; total T. (f) Write a formula for T in terms of d and h","answer":"(a) e^5 (b) 3m (c) 6g² (d) a²+8a (e) 5(3x+4) (f) T=3d+5h","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"fa9","topic":"factorising","ref":"Nov 2023 2F Q12","q":"(a) Expand x(x+3). (b) Factorise 8p+10. (c) Make e the subject of y=eh-f. Janya's whole number w satisfies w>7 and w≤10. (d) Write down the possible values of w","answer":"(a) x²+3x (b) 2(4p+5) (c) e=(y+f)/h (d) w = 8, 9, 10","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"fa10","topic":"factorising","ref":"June 2023 2F Q13","q":"(a) Expand x(3-x). (b) Factorise fully 12a-18b. There are 8 slices per small pack of cheese and 20 per large pack. Afreen buys h small packs and j large packs, a total of T slices. (c) Write down a formula for T in terms of h and j","answer":"(a) 3x-x² (b) 6(2a-3b) (c) T=8h+20j","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"fa11","topic":"factorising","ref":"June 2022 2F Q11","q":"(a) Simplify c×c×c×c×c×c. (b) Simplify 2h^3+5h^3-h^3. (c) Expand x(x+5). (d) Factorise 9y-12. Rosanna sells m small bags (15 marbles each) and p large bags (40 marbles each) of marbles; total T. (e) Write a formula for T in terms of m and p","answer":"(a) c^6 (b) 6h³ (c) x²+5x (d) 3(3y-4) (e) T=15m+40p","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"fa12","topic":"factorising","ref":"Jan 2022 1F Q21","q":"(a) Solve the inequality 5x-7≤2. (b)(i) Factorise y^2-2y-35. (ii) Hence, solve y^2-2y-35=0","answer":"(a) 5x≤9, x≤9/5 (1.8) (b)(i) (y-7)(y+5) (ii) y=7 or y=-5","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) 5x-7≤2 → 5x≤9 → x≤1.8"]},{"id":"fa13","topic":"factorising","ref":"Jan 2022 2F Q16","q":"(a) Expand and simplify x(2x-3)+7(2x+1)-5. (b) Expand and simplify (y+4)(2-y). (c) Factorise fully 15b^5c-35b^3c^9","answer":"(a) 2x²-3x+14x+7-5 = 2x²+11x+2 (b) 2y-y²+8-4y = -y²-2y+8 (c) 5b³c(3b²-7c^8)","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) x(2x-3)=2x²-3x; 7(2x+1)=14x+7; sum minus 5: 2x²-3x+14x+7-5=2x²+11x+2"]},{"id":"fa14","topic":"factorising","ref":"June 2026 2F Q26","q":"(a) Find the value of 7n^0 where n>0. (b) Simplify fully (2m^5p^4)^3. (c) Factorise fully 18c^5w^2+30cw^3. (d) Factorise x^2+6x-27","answer":"(a) 7 (b) 8m^15p^12 (c) 6cw²(3c^4+5w) (d) (x+9)(x-3)","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"fa15","topic":"factorising","ref":"Nov 2024 2F Q8","q":"(a) Simplify 7g+3h+4g-5h. (b) Simplify 7a×4m. (c) Solve 5x-7=12. (d) Expand 5(7k+3). (e) Factorise 9y+12. Max has c counters; Bulan has 3 times as many as Max; Chanda has 7 more than Max. (f) Write an expression, in terms of c, for the total counters Max, Bulan and Chanda have, simplified.","answer":"(a) 11g-2h (b) 28am (c) x=19/5 (3.8) (d) 35k+15 (e) 3(3y+4) (f) c+3c+(c+7) = 5c+7","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"fa16","topic":"factorising","ref":"June 2023 1F Q21","q":"(a) Simplify (2c^4d^7)^3. (b) Find the value of 5y^0 where y>0. (c) Factorise fully 16a^2b^3+20a^3b. (d)(i) Factorise x^2+9x-22. (ii) Hence solve x^2+9x-22=0","answer":"(a) 8c^12d^21 (b) 5 (c) 4a²b(4b²+5a) (d)(i) (x+11)(x-2) (ii) x=-11 or x=2","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"fa17","topic":"factorising","ref":"Nov 2025 1H Q21","q":"Express 5x^2 - 20x + 23 in the form a(x-b)^2 + c where a, b and c are integers.","answer":"5x²-20x+23 = 5(x²-4x)+23 = 5[(x-2)²-4]+23 = 5(x-2)²+3, so a=5, b=2, c=3","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["5x²-20x+23 = 5(x²-4x)+23","Complete the square: x²-4x = (x-2)²-4","5[(x-2)²-4]+23 = 5(x-2)²-20+23 = 5(x-2)²+3"]},{"id":"fa18","topic":"factorising","ref":"June 2025 2H Q12","q":"Expand and simplify 3x(2x+5)(7x-4)","answer":"(2x+5)(7x-4) = 14x²+27x-20, then 3x×(14x²+27x-20) = 42x³+81x²-60x","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(2x+5)(7x-4) = 14x²-8x+35x-20 = 14x²+27x-20","3x(14x²+27x-20) = 42x³+81x²-60x"]},{"id":"fa19","topic":"factorising","ref":"Nov 2023 2H Q16","q":"Expand and simplify (2x+3)(x-5)(x+4)","answer":"(x-5)(x+4) = x²-x-20, then (2x+3)(x²-x-20) = 2x³+x²-43x-60","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(x-5)(x+4) = x²-x-20","(2x+3)(x²-x-20) = 2x³-2x²-40x+3x²-3x-60 = 2x³+x²-43x-60"]},{"id":"fa20","topic":"factorising","ref":"June 2023 1H Q14","q":"Factorise fully 50g^2-18","answer":"50g²-18 = 2(25g²-9) = 2(5g-3)(5g+3)","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Take out factor 2: 2(25g²-9)","25g²-9 is a difference of squares: (5g-3)(5g+3)"]},{"id":"fa21","topic":"factorising","ref":"June 2023 2H Q19","q":"Express 3x^2-6x+5 in the form a(x-b)^2+c","answer":"3x²-6x+5 = 3(x²-2x)+5 = 3[(x-1)²-1]+5 = 3(x-1)²+2, so a=3, b=1, c=2","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["3x²-6x+5 = 3(x²-2x)+5","x²-2x = (x-1)²-1","3[(x-1)²-1]+5 = 3(x-1)²+2"]},{"id":"fa22","topic":"factorising","ref":"Jan 2022 2H Q1","q":"(a) Expand and simplify (y+4)(2-y). (b) Factorise fully 15b^5c-35b^3c^9","answer":"(a) 2y-y²+8-4y = -y²-2y+8 (b) 5b³c(3b²-7c^8)","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"fa23","topic":"factorising","ref":"Nov 2025 1H Q14","q":"(a) Expand and simplify 7x(3x+2)(2x-5). (b) Solve 9/(2y)+5/7=5. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"(a) (3x+2)(2x-5)=6x²-11x-10, then 7x(6x²-11x-10)=42x³-77x²-70x (b) multiply by 14y: 63+10y=70y → 63=60y → y=21/20 (1.05)","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) (3x+2)(2x-5)=6x²-15x+4x-10=6x²-11x-10; 7x×(6x²-11x-10)=42x³-77x²-70x","(b) Multiply through by 14y: 63+10y=70y → 63=60y → y=63/60=21/20"]},{"id":"fa24","topic":"factorising","ref":"Nov 2024 1H Q15","q":"Write 3x(2x-1)(5x+4) in the form ax^3+bx^2+cx where a, b and c are integers.","answer":"(2x-1)(5x+4)=10x²+3x-4, then 3x(10x²+3x-4)=30x³+9x²-12x, so a=30, b=9, c=-12","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(2x-1)(5x+4) = 10x²+8x-5x-4 = 10x²+3x-4","3x(10x²+3x-4) = 30x³+9x²-12x"]},{"id":"fa25","topic":"factorising","ref":"June 2024 1H Q25","q":"f(x) = 17 - 3x^2 + 12x. Write f(x) in the form a - b(x-c)^2 where a, b and c are constants.","answer":"f(x)=-3x²+12x+17=-3(x²-4x)+17=-3[(x-2)²-4]+17=-3(x-2)²+29, so a=29, b=3, c=2","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["f(x) = -3x²+12x+17 = -3(x²-4x)+17","x²-4x = (x-2)²-4","-3[(x-2)²-4]+17 = -3(x-2)²+12+17 = -3(x-2)²+29"]},{"id":"fa26","topic":"factorising","ref":"Jan 2023 1H Q13","q":"Expand and simplify 3x(2x-5)^2. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"(2x-5)²=4x²-20x+25, then 3x(4x²-20x+25) = 12x³-60x²+75x","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(2x-5)² = 4x²-20x+25","3x(4x²-20x+25) = 12x³-60x²+75x"]},{"id":"fa27","topic":"factorising","ref":"Jan 2022 1H Q13","q":"(a) Expand and simplify 5x(x+2)(3x-4). (b) Simplify completely (16w^8/y^20)^(-3/4)","answer":"(a) (x+2)(3x-4)=3x²+2x-8, then 5x(3x²+2x-8)=15x³+10x²-40x (b) = y^15/(8w^6)","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) (x+2)(3x-4)=3x²-4x+6x-8=3x²+2x-8; 5x(3x²+2x-8)=15x³+10x²-40x","(b) (16w^8/y^20)^(-3/4) = (y^20/16w^8)^(3/4) = y^15/(16^(3/4)w^6) = y^15/(8w^6), since 16^(3/4)=8"]},{"id":"fa28","topic":"factorising","ref":"Jan 2022 1H Q20","q":"(a) Express 7+12x-3x^2 in the form a+b(x+c)^2 where a, b and c are integers. C is the curve y=7+12x-3x^2, with maximum point A. (b) Use your answer to part (a) to write down the coordinates of A","answer":"(a) 7+12x-3x² = -3(x-2)²+19, so a=19, b=-3, c=-2 (b) A = (2, 19)","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["-3x²+12x+7 = -3(x²-4x)+7 = -3[(x-2)²-4]+7 = -3(x-2)²+19","Maximum point: x=2, y=19"]},{"id":"fa29","topic":"factorising","ref":"June 2026 1H Q24","q":"(a) Express 10-24x-3x^2 in the form a-b(x+c)^2 where a, b and c are integers. T is the curve y=10-24(x-1)-3(x-1)^2, with maximum point P. (b) Use your answer to part (a) to find the coordinates of P. (c) Write down the equation of the line of symmetry of T","answer":"(a) 10-24x-3x² = 58-3(x+4)², so a=58, b=3, c=4 (b) Substituting X=x-1 into 58-3(X+4)² gives y=58-3(x+3)², so maximum at P=(-3, 58) (c) x = -3","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["10-24x-3x² = -3(x²+8x)+10 = -3[(x+4)²-16]+10 = 58-3(x+4)²","T uses (x-1) in place of x: y=58-3((x-1)+4)²=58-3(x+3)²","Maximum point P: x+3=0 → x=-3, y=58, so P=(-3,58); line of symmetry x=-3"]},{"id":"fa30","topic":"factorising","ref":"June 2025 2H Q25","q":"(a) Write 28+24x-6x^2 in the form a-b(x-c)^2 where a, b and c are integers. (b) On axes, sketch the graph of y=28+24x-6x^2, showing the turning point and the y-intercept.","answer":"(a) 28+24x-6x² = 52-6(x-2)², so a=52, b=6, c=2 (b) Turning point (maximum) at (2, 52); curve crosses the y-axis at (0, 28); a downward (n-shaped) parabola through these points","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["28+24x-6x² = -6(x²-4x)+28 = -6[(x-2)²-4]+28 = -6(x-2)²+52","Turning point (2,52); y-intercept: x=0 → y=28, point (0,28)"]},{"id":"fa31","topic":"factorising","ref":"June 2023 2H Q17","q":"(a) Expand and simplify (x+6)(3x-2)(x+6). (b) Make e the subject of w = sqrt((e+g)/(ef-d))","answer":"(a) 3x³+34x²+84x-72 (b) e = (g+w²d)/(w²f-1)","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) (x+6)² = x²+12x+36; ×(3x-2) = 3x³-2x²+36x²-24x+108x-72 = 3x³+34x²+84x-72","(b) Square both sides: w² = (e+g)/(ef-d) → w²(ef-d) = e+g → w²ef - w²d = e+g → e(w²f-1) = g+w²d → e = (g+w²d)/(w²f-1)"]},{"id":"fa32","topic":"factorising","ref":"June 2022 1H Q24","q":"Express each of a, b and c in terms of q so that q+12x-qx^2 can be written as a-b(x-c)^2","answer":"q+12x-qx² = -q(x-6/q)² + q + 36/q, so a = q+36/q, b = q, c = 6/q","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["q+12x-qx² = -q(x²-12x/q)+q = -q[(x-6/q)²-36/q²]+q = -q(x-6/q)²+36/q+q","So a=q+36/q, b=q, c=6/q"]},{"id":"fa33","topic":"factorising","ref":"June 2022 2H Q14","q":"(a) Expand and simplify (5-x)(2x+3)(x+4). (b) Make c the subject of g=(c+3)/(4+c) - 7","answer":"(a) -2x³-x²+43x+60 (b) c = -(4g+25)/(g+6)","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) (2x+3)(x+4)=2x²+11x+12; (5-x)(2x²+11x+12)=10x²+55x+60-2x³-11x²-12x=-2x³-x²+43x+60","(b) g+7=(c+3)/(4+c) → (g+7)(4+c)=c+3 → 4g+28+gc+7c=c+3 → c(g+6)=-4g-25 → c=-(4g+25)/(g+6)"]},{"id":"af1","topic":"algfrac","ref":"June 2026 1F Q13","q":"(a) Factorise 15y-20. (b) Solve 5w+2=3w-7","answer":"(a) 5(3y-4) (b) w = -4.5","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["5w+2=3w-7","5w-3w=-7-2","2w=-9, so w=-4.5"]},{"id":"af2","topic":"algfrac","ref":"June 2024 1F Q21","q":"(a) Expand and simplify (m+5)(m-8). (b) Solve 3n-4=(5n+6)/3","answer":"(a) m²-3m-40 (b) n = 4.5","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) (m+5)(m-8) = m²-8m+5m-40 = m²-3m-40","(b) Multiply by 3: 9n-12=5n+6 → 4n=18 → n=4.5"]},{"id":"af3","topic":"algfrac","ref":"June 2022 1F Q20","q":"(a) Expand and simplify (n-6)(n+4). (b) Solve 2x-3=(3x-5)/4","answer":"(a) n²-2n-24 (b) x = 1.4","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) (n-6)(n+4) = n²+4n-6n-24 = n²-2n-24","(b) Multiply by 4: 8x-12=3x-5 → 5x=7 → x=1.4"]},{"id":"af4","topic":"algfrac","ref":"Jan 2022 2FR Q20","q":"(a) Solve the inequality 4y+5>12. (b) Solve 6x-5=(4x-7)/2","answer":"(a) y > 1.75 (b) x = 0.375","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) 4y+5>12 → 4y>7 → y>1.75","(b) Multiply by 2: 12x-10=4x-7 → 8x=3 → x=0.375"]},{"id":"af5","topic":"algfrac","ref":"June 2022 2FR Q23","q":"(a) Solve p=(3p-5)/10. (b) Find the value of a^0 where a>0. (c) Simplify fully 3xy^3/(6x^2y). (d) Factorise fully 10c^3d^2+15cd^4","answer":"(a) p = -5/7 (b) 1 (c) y²/(2x) (d) 5cd²(2c²+3d²)","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) Multiply by 10: 10p=3p-5 → 7p=-5 → p=-5/7","(c) 3xy³/(6x²y) = y^(3-1)/(2x^(2-1)) = y²/(2x)","(d) HCF of 10c³d² and 15cd⁴ is 5cd²: 5cd²(2c²+3d²)"]},{"id":"af6","topic":"algfrac","ref":"June 2025 1H Q12","q":"Express 5/4 + (x-3)/(6x) as a single fraction in its simplest form.","answer":"(17x-6)/(12x)","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Common denominator 12x: 5/4 = 15x/12x and (x-3)/(6x) = (2x-6)/12x","Add: (15x + 2x-6)/12x = (17x-6)/(12x)"]},{"id":"af7","topic":"algfrac","ref":"Nov 2023 1H Q11","q":"Express 3/4 + (5-x)/(6x) as a single fraction in its simplest terms.","answer":"(7x+10)/(12x)","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Common denominator 12x: 3/4 = 9x/12x and (5-x)/(6x) = (10-2x)/12x","Add: (9x + 10-2x)/12x = (7x+10)/(12x)"]}];